= The Trial of Max Hoelz

Max Hoelz was arrested in Berlin in April, living under a false name. He is tried before a special court in Moabit. He does not defend himself; he accuses. He tells the court about prisoners beaten and shot in March, about the Kapp officers who were never punished, about the hunger in the Vogtland.

On 22 June he is sentenced to penal servitude for life, for a murder he almost certainly did not commit. The courtroom sings the Internationale as he is taken out.

[? if march_action = 0 : He fought in March without us, against our advice. The workers of Central Germany do not care about that. ?][? if march_action = 1 : Hundreds of our own comrades are going through the same courts this summer, with less publicity and similar sentences. ?]

- @campaign: Make him a symbol: a national campaign for Hoelz.
- @relief: Build a relief organisation for all the prisoners.
- @distance: Keep our distance from a bank robber.

@campaign
subtitle: The Left's line. Hoelz is popular, and so is defiance.
on-arrival: worker_support += 2; militancy += 3; offensive_satisfaction += 5; luxemburgist_satisfaction -= 2; lean_offensive += 1

"Free Max Hoelz" is painted on walls from Plauen to Hamburg. The campaign will last for years.

@relief
